# Build directories. One pattern for every separator the docs and CI use:
# `build/`, `build_gpu/`, and `build-gpu/` (the name INSTALL.md and the
# gpu-portable-isa CI job teach). The previous `build/` + `build_*/` pair
# missed the hyphen, so `build-gpu/` showed up as untracked in every status.
# Trailing slash: directories only, so scripts/build_lola_ring.py is untouched.
build*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile

# Compiled object files
*.o
# `*.obj` is a C/C++ object-file rule that also matches every Wavefront OBJ
# shape model in the tree. The curated body cache ships shape models
# there, so they are excepted BY NAME rather than force-added: a force-add is
# invisible to the next person, and the day someone re-adds one without -f it
# would silently stop being tracked -- leaving a curated card that offers a
# file no fresh checkout contains. No parent directory of these paths is
# excluded, which is what makes the negations take effect.
#
# ONE LINE PER SHIPPED SHAPE, deliberately, rather than un-ignoring the whole
# directory: scripts/fetch_data.py downloads OPTIONAL higher-resolution shape
# models (bennu-shape-hires, 14 MB) into this same directory, and a directory
# -wide negation would offer those to the next `git add -A`. Adding a curated
# body is already a multi-file act (see gui/gui_core/curated_sources.py,
# "Adding a body"); this is one more line of it.
#
# THE POLICY these lines implement: a shape model that a committed configuration
# loads is a production input, so it is TRACKED, it carries a named exception
# here, and it carries a provenance sidecar next to it (source, version, URL,
# md5, date) plus a PROVENANCE.md in its body directory. The exception is by
# EXACT FILENAME so that removing a shape and leaving the rule behind is
# visible. See data/horizons_cache/README.md, "Shape-model policy".
*.obj
# (101955) Bennu -- OSIRIS-REx OLA v21 global model, and the superseded Nolan
# 2013 radar model kept because a shipped notebook reads it by name.
!data/horizons_cache/bodies/**/bennu_radar_shape.obj
!data/horizons_cache/bodies/**/g_06370mm_alt_obj_0000n00000_v021.obj
# (269) Justitia -- DAMIT model 2858, the original, plus the
# 2026-07-04 hand reconstruction it replaced. The reconstruction is retained for
# the same reason Bennu's radar model is: it is the shape behind every Justitia
# product made before 2026-08-31. The two are geometrically identical (max
# vertex deviation 0.000000000 km); see this body's PROVENANCE.md.
!data/horizons_cache/bodies/269_Justitia_(A887_SA)/shape.obj
!data/horizons_cache/bodies/269_Justitia_(A887_SA)/shape_reconstructed_20260704.obj
# (623) Chimaera -- DAMIT model 9110, plus the 2-pass Loop-subdivided mesh that
# this body's body_config.yaml actually loads. The subdivider is NOT in this
# repository, so the refined mesh cannot be regenerated from tracked source.
!data/horizons_cache/bodies/623_Chimaera_(A907_BC)/shape.obj
!data/horizons_cache/bodies/623_Chimaera_(A907_BC)/shape_refined.obj
*.so
*.dll
*.dylib
*.a

# scripts/ptm12_diag compiled diagnostic binaries. These build with a bare
# `c++ ... -o mc_ref_pp` (no CMake target, no extension), so none of the
# patterns above catch them, and a bare `git add -A`/`git add scripts/` would
# happily stage a compiled artifact -- exactly the "stale untracked binary"
# trap this repo already paid for once (mc_ref_pp compiled 2026-07-23,
# predating the back-face-cull fix 44210d8/ce3ca8c, silently reused by
# run_pp_sweep.sh). It and its build cache must always be rebuilt from
# mc_ref_pp.cpp via scripts/ptm12_diag/ensure_mc_ref_pp.py, never committed.
scripts/ptm12_diag/mc_ref_pp
scripts/ptm12_diag/.mc_ref_pp_cache/

